 "note": "From pi-anton-fob's draft (anton-fob 436ea2f hardware/keychain-board), with library parts and fixes: D2 K only on GND (was on GND and STATUS2), LDO EN on VBAT (was on the module's EN), charger STAT on IO4 (IO43 is TXD0), USB on the module's USB_D+/USB_D- (IO20/IO19), AMC7135 3-pin SOT-89 with VDD from IO1 (PWM), the cell on a JST SH 2-pin. AMC7135 pin order (1 OUT, 2 GND, 3 VDD) to be checked against its datasheet. Placement (try 3): the module's antenna at the top edge (its keepout spans the board's width), the ICs, two rows of passives, the buttons and the torch, then USB-C with its mouth at the bottom edge, the cell's JST and the status LED; courtyards from the 9.0.9 footprints. 3D: U1 is Espressif's own ESP32-S3-MINI-1 model (KiCad's library has none for the S2/S3-MINI-1), offset -7.7, -10.25, 0 mm: the model's origin is its corner (0..15.4 x 0..20.5 mm), Espressif's own footprint places it at -7.7, -7.7 and has its pads 2.55 mm higher than KiCad's, so on KiCad's footprint the body is centred as the footprint's fab outline (±7.7 x ±10.25); D1 is a 3.5 x 3.5 mm PLCC body as a stand-in for the 3535 torch LED (no model for LED_Cree-XP), for the case fit only."
